   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Background and Prior Work \n"
    "Choosing a major is one of the most important decisions college students make. This choice impacts their future careers and their development as a person. There are many factors that one considers when taking into account what they want to study such as high school classes interests, what their family members studied, and many more. For our project we want to investigate if there are any subconscious influences when choosing a major. To do so, we want to see if there is a correlation between a student's music taste and major election. \n",
    "\n",
    "A study pertaining to music taste and personality showed that people with certain personality traits tend to enjoy certain music genres more than others <a name=\"cite_ref-1\"></a>[<sup>1</sup>](#cite_note-1). This study showed that music is somehow embedded in certain personality traits of people. Similarly, other studies found out that personality traits do play a role when choosing a college major <a name=\"cite_ref-2\"></a>[<sup>2</sup>](#cite_note-2). Both of these studies are making reference to the “Big Five Personality Traits”. By seeing that personality is related to both music and major choice, we want to discover the relationship between both or if it is solely the personality and music taste that is not really reflected among majors.\n",
    "\n",
    "The relationship between music taste and other life aspects has been studied before as well. For instance, a study looked at the relationship between music taste and job choice and they found there was a relation between both <a name=\"cite_ref-3\"></a>[<sup>3</sup>](#cite_note-3). There has been previous research on topics where music taste is used to evaluate people’s decision making. This research study is important because it shows that music can be related to people’s life and career so based on this we want to explore how music plays a role before choosing a job. \n",
    "\n",
    "The research conducted introduced some critical points that bring to light how music choice can play a role in influencing an individual's personality. While they all highlight the connection between music preferences and various aspects of an individual's life, the relationship is not yet fully understood. \n",
    "\n",
    "This gap in understanding presents an opportunity for further exploration into how music taste could be a significant, yet subconscious, influence on a student's selection of a college major. To better address this we plan on diversifying our sample pool to be more representative of the population of students at UC San Diego and within our data collection method we plan on repurposing some of the strategies implemented by the Humburg study to understand how we can structure our questionnaire to collect data regarding the effect of the big five personality traits. By refining our methodology and broadening our sample, we aim to uncover how music preferences may guide the academic and professional paths students choose, providing deeper insights into the intersection between personality, music taste, and educational decisions. \n",
    "\n",
    "<a name=\"cite_note-1\"></a> [1.](#cite_ref-1) Nave, G. et. al. (2018). Musical Preferences Predict Personality: Evidence From Active Listening and Facebook Likes. Psychological science, 29(7), 1145–1158. https://doi.org/10.1177/0956797618761659 \n",
    "\n",
    "<a name=\"cite_note-2\"></a> [2.](#cite_ref-2) Humburg, M. (2012). The Effect of the Big Five Personality Traits on College Major Choice : Evidence from a Dutch longitudinal youth cohort study. The Society of Labor Economists, 1-20. https://www.sole-jole.org/assets/docs/13190.pdf\n",
    "\n",
    "<a name='cite_note-3'></a> [3.](#cite_ref-3) Kno, D. (2016). What your job reveals about the music you listen to, indy100.https://www.indy100.com/news/what-your-job-reveals-about-the-music-you-listen-to-7427961"
 
   ]
  },
